cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "auction-lab: step-through visualizations of auction mechanisms"
message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Filippou
    given-names: Michail
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7388-0680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/choosen23/auction-lab"
url: "https://auctionlab.dev"
# The concept DOI — resolves to the latest archived version on Zenodo.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22246375
abstract: >-
  auction-lab renders auction mechanisms as inspectable sequences of
  algorithmic steps. It covers single-item mechanisms (first-price,
  second-price, all-pay, English, Dutch), position auctions (GSP, VCG),
  combinatorial auctions with greedy and optimal winner determination,
  repeated-round bidder strategies with budget pacing and learning agents,
  and pure-strategy equilibrium analysis including revenue equivalence.
  The engine is pure Python standard library; the interface is dependency-free
  JavaScript.
keywords:
  - auction theory
  - mechanism design
  - algorithmic game theory
  - Vickrey auction
  - VCG
  - generalized second-price auction
  - combinatorial auction
  - teaching
license: MIT
